er them in  in ilink many many times and then i  listen when i go running and so all of  this is just kind of letting all the  language wash over me occasionally  reviewing them in flashcards so and i've  been doing mostly that and plus also  reading uh  this czech newspaper which i have online  here which i go to every day and read  i use the the link bookmarklet to bring  in  this is uh  novini  and so here's an article  conference  marzenic  fondue i understand that all and i read  the article and there's words that i  don't understand but they want to  unblock the  frozen funds and so forth  but  and that's just text that i read but i  find now that i'm able to read these  newspaper articles  you know not too bad i  you know my my text and link is covered  in yellow highlighted words because  these are words that i've looked up and  i'm seeing again and again and again and  they're gradually starting to stick  but in radio praha when i listen to  those articles even though i've read  them and saved the words and studied  them when i hear it you know i  understand 30 40  so when i got back to this uh check for  beginners whatever it was here with two  the cds the hippocrene books of course i  understood just about everything but  there were still a few words that i  didn't understand and then i would read  the text  and i'd ah now i understand yeah it's  that word i didn't quite make it out  when i was listening and i listen again  i still miss it  so then i started saying to myself am i  better off to spend a lot of time trying  to nail down everything and that's in  these 10  lessons in this beginner book or am i  better off to continue  listening to radio praha reading the  transcripts saving the words and phrases  going off to the uh  the czech newspaper jessica novini  and reading more articles about vatslav  krauss and his latest outrageous  statements or whatever  and  doing a bit of  fake and just letting the words wash  over me  because on the one hand d